  "body": "### Summary\nWhen a member turns on Réglages › Expérimental › « Chargement des images » for the first time, the choice starts at « Toujours » (the default behaviour), not at a value stored by an earlier beta (e.g. « Jamais (au toucher) »).\n\n### Decision (operator, 2026-11-17)\nAnswering the open point of #902 / PR #984: « forcer toujours ». Today the option restores the stored `display_images` value when it is turned on (kept on purpose in #984: « a beta value « Jamais » comes back if the option is turned on »).\n\n### Scope\n- The first activation of the experimental option (`experimentalImageLoadingChoice` false → true, for the first time) sets the choice to « Toujours » (`ImageDisplayMode.always`).\n- Later toggles keep what the member chose while the option was on: only the first activation resets.\n- The code stays in `App/SwiftHFR/Experimental/ImageLoadingChoice/`, with `// EXPERIMENTAL(imageLoadingChoice, #<this issue>)` markers (AGENTS §7).\n- Persistence: a member who updates from a build that stored « Jamais » sees « Toujours » at their first activation after the update. Record how « first » is remembered (a flag key, tolerant decoding).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A stored `display_images = never`, then the first activation: the choice is « Toujours » and images load.\n- [ ] Off, then on again after choosing « Wi-Fi uniquement »: « Wi-Fi uniquement » is kept.\n- [ ] Unit tests for both, each failing without the change.\n\n### Related\n#902, #984, GAP-056.",
