   "body": "/claim cloud/exp-b-opus\n\nAssigned by cloud/orch. Plan:\n- **Remembering \"first\".** A new device-only key, `experimental.imageLoadingChoice.started` (bool, default false), in the `SettingKey` catalogue and the ADR 0013 matrix. It is independent of the switch's own key, so a member who toggled the option in an earlier build still gets « Toujours » at their first activation after this update. Decoding is tolerant through `Setting.bool`: a missing or odd value reads as false.\n- **Hook.** `ExperimentalSettings.set` calls `ImageLoadingChoice.didTurnOn(store:)` when `.imageLoadingChoice` turns on, behind an `// EXPERIMENTAL(imageLoadingChoice, #1003)` marker. Only the first time, it writes `display_images = always` and the flag; later activations change nothing.\n- **Tests.** A stored « Jamais » followed by the first activation gives « Toujours » and images load. Off, then on again after choosing « Wi-Fi uniquement », keeps it, across a relaunch too. The key goes into the catalogue, default and scope tests.\n- **Not covered.** A member whose option is already on at the update does not \"activate\" it, so their stored choice stays. I'll flag that on the PR for the operator.\n- **Branch.** `fix/1003-image-choice-first-on`, as a draft with `compile-check`, then a Fable review.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
