   "body": "**Open question for the operator** (from the review of #1004, kept here so it outlives the PR):\n\nTwo cases are not settled by the decision « forcer toujours ». #1004 handles both as described below, and its tests pin that behaviour.\n\n1. **The option was on in a build since #984 (2026-11-17) with a choice made there, e.g. « Wi-Fi uniquement ».**\n   - #1004 follows the persistence point: the first activation after the update, meaning off then on, gives « Toujours ».\n   - The alternative is to count the first turning-off after the update as \"already started\" and keep the earlier choice. That would also keep a stored « Jamais ».\n2. **The option is still on at the update and is never turned off and on again.** No activation happens, so the stored choice, « Jamais » included, stays.\n   - The alternative is a launch-time reset when the option is on and the flag is absent.\n\nAnswer here and I'll apply it in a small follow-up. Either answer shows up in `ImageLoadingChoiceTests.anActivationBeforeTheUpdateDoesNotCount(wasOn:)`.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
